Subject: [PATCH] sixaxis: trust controllers once cable pairing is authorized

Sixaxis controllers never bond. Without the trusted flag, BlueZ asks the
agent again on every Bluetooth connection, and removes the (unbonded) device
as soon as one connection attempt fails, so the pad has to be paired again.

Mark the device trusted once the cable pairing has been authorized.

Tested: pad trusted at pairing, kept after a disconnection, reconnects with
no prompt.
---
--- a/plugins/sixaxis.c
+++ b/plugins/sixaxis.c
@@ -297,6 +297,12 @@
 	remove_device = false;
 	btd_device_set_temporary(closure->device, false);
 
+	/* The user authorized this controller over a cable, so trust it:
+	 * it can't bond, and an untrusted device would be asked for
+	 * authorization on every connection and removed if one fails.
+	 */
+	btd_device_set_trusted(closure->device, true);
+
 	if (closure->type == CABLE_PAIRING_SIXAXIS) {
 		btd_device_set_record(closure->device, HID_UUID,
 						 SIXAXIS_HID_SDP_RECORD);
